# All four images (backend + the three Streamlit UIs) build with the repo root
# as their context — the backend so LICENSE/NOTICE ship inside it (AGPL §4), the
# UIs so the shared content-sdk package is reachable. Docker reads the context
# root's .dockerignore, so this file is the *only* one in effect. A
# .dockerignore sitting in apps/<app>/ is never consulted — Docker would read
# apps/<app>/Dockerfile.dockerignore, which is not how they were named — so the
# four per-app copies were removed rather than left looking authoritative.
# Everything they covered is folded in below.
#
# Every Dockerfile COPYs explicit paths, never `COPY .`. The exclusions below
# keep the context lean and make a future `COPY .` non-catastrophic.
.git

# Local secrets must never reach a build context, even though no Dockerfile
# COPYs them today — the next `COPY .` would be the mistake.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.claude/
secrets/

# Virtualenvs, bytecode, tool caches and editable-install metadata. Anchored
# with **/ because these exist per-app, not only at the root.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Runtime state: the SQLite database, artifacts and the analysis cache. Both the
# root store and the backend's own live under a `data/` folder.
**/data/

# Test suites: no image COPYs them, and apps/backend/tests alone is 2.4 MB.
**/tests/

# Local-only or non-shipped material.
playground/
work/
docs/
hometube/
